Foot of the Lighthouse
A spiral stair climbs into the dark.  The door leads back out, to the south.

The old keeper is here.

>x keeper
The keeper is old and grey-bearded, and he is shivering.

>talk to keeper
“Thank goodness,” the keeper says.  “My legs won’t take the stairs tonight.”

>ask keeper about storm
“Worst I’ve seen,” he says.  “There’ll be ships out there.”

>ask keeper about lamp
“It’s at the top of the stair,” he says.  “Just switch it on.”

>ask keeper about fish
The keeper only shakes his head.

